# meridian.spline — a freeform b-spline cavity meridian for spline_funnel.cam.
# The (r, z) control polygon of a cubic funnel of revolution, in mm, stored
# MOUTH-FIRST (mouth rim widest, in the stock-top plane; tip circle at the
# bottom). Both coordinate sequences are monotone — r non-increasing, z
# non-increasing — so the revolved cavity is machinable with no undercut (the
# mirror of the cap's apex-first envelope). Genuinely freeform, mixed
# curvature (a concave upper wall rolling through an inflection into a convex
# flare above the tip), so recognition cannot name it as a primitive: the
# analytic reader's cavity counterpart. The open tip (r=5) carries the
# stated tip-relief assumption — see the .cam file.
degree 3
knots 0 0 0 0 0.3333333333333333 0.6666666666666666 1 1 1 1
pole 13 0
pole 12 -3
pole 10 -8
pole 8 -12
pole 6 -15
pole 5 -18
